slug: stroke-syndromes-by-territory
title: Stroke Syndromes: Read the Artery from the Body
area: Neurology
level: Clinical
best: 3rd year onwards
minutes: 16
hook: Face and arm weak with language gone, or only the leg, or only the vision? The pattern on the body tells you which artery is blocked. Block each artery yourself and watch the body map change. || Chehra aur bazoo kamzor aur zubaan ghayab, ya sirf taang, ya sirf nazar? Jism ka pattern batata hai kaunsi artery band hai. Har artery khud band karein aur body map badalta dekhein.
goal: By the end, you'll link MCA, ACA, PCA, lateral medullary and lacunar strokes to their typical deficits, tell left from right hemisphere problems, and shape a physiotherapy plan around each pattern. || End tak aap MCA, ACA, PCA, lateral medullary aur lacunar strokes ko un ke aam nuqs se jorenge, left aur right hemisphere ke masail alag karenge, aur har pattern ke mutabiq physiotherapy plan banayenge.

say: A stroke is a map-reading problem. Each artery feeds a fixed **territory**, so the deficit is a fingerprint of the vessel. The **middle cerebral artery (MCA)** feeds the side of the brain: face, arm, language, spatial attention. The **anterior cerebral artery (ACA)** feeds the inner surface, where the leg lives. The **posterior cerebral artery (PCA)** feeds the back of the brain: vision and the thalamus. Deep small vessels (lacunes) and the **vertebrobasilar** system (brainstem, cerebellum) complete the picture. || Stroke ek map parhne ka masla hai. Har artery ek muqarrar **territory** ko khoon deti hai, is liye nuqs us nali ka fingerprint hota hai. **Middle cerebral artery (MCA)** dimagh ki side ko khilati hai: chehra, bazoo, zubaan, spatial attention. **Anterior cerebral artery (ACA)** andar wali surface ko, jahan taang rehti hai. **Posterior cerebral artery (PCA)** dimagh ke pichlay hissay ko: nazar aur thalamus. Gehri chhoti nalian (lacunes) aur **vertebrobasilar** system (brainstem, cerebellum) tasveer mukammal karte hain.
analogy: Think of **three canals irrigating a city**. The big central canal (MCA) waters the wide middle districts, so blocking it ruins the busiest neighbourhoods: face, arm, speech. The thin canal running down the middle strip (ACA) waters a narrow lane where the legs live. The canal at the back (PCA) waters the observation tower: the eyes. Where the canal is blocked, only that district dries up. || **Shehar ki teen nehrein** tasawwur karein. Bari central nehar (MCA) kushada darmiyani ilaqon ko seeraab karti hai, is liye band hone par sab se masroof mohalle (chehra, bazoo, bolna) barbaad. Darmiyan ki patli patti wali nehar (ACA) ek tang gali ko seeraab karti hai jahan taangein rehti hain. Peechay ki nehar (PCA) nigrani ke burj, yaani aankhon, ko seeraab karti hai. Jahan nehar band, sirf wohi ilaqa sookhta hai.
widget: stroke-territories :: Choose an artery and a side. The brain is drawn from above, so the patient's right is on the left of the picture. Notice that cortical and deep strokes show on the OPPOSITE body, but the lateral medullary stroke breaks the rule: face on the lesion side, body on the other. Switch between the left and right hemisphere on the MCA and see which "extra" problem appears. || Artery aur side chunein. Dimagh upar se dikhaya gaya hai, is liye patient ka right tasveer ke left par hai. Dekhein ke cortical aur deep strokes ULTI side ke jism par dikhte hain, magar lateral medullary stroke yeh usool tod deta hai: chehra lesion ki side, jism doosri side. MCA par left aur right hemisphere badal kar dekhein ke kaunsa "extra" masla aata hai.
check: A man has a sudden weak left leg, a mildly weak left arm, loses his drive and cannot control his bladder. His face and speech are normal. Which artery? || Ek aadmi ki achanak left taang kamzor, left bazoo halka kamzor, hosla khatam aur bladder par qaboo nahi. Chehra aur bolna normal. Kaunsi artery?
ok: Right anterior cerebral artery || Right anterior cerebral artery || Yes — a leg-predominant weakness with apathy (abulia) and incontinence is the classic ACA picture: the leg area and frontal control sit on the inner surface. || Haan — taang par zyada kamzori, bedili (abulia) aur incontinence classic ACA tasveer hai: taang ka ilaqa aur frontal control andar wali surface par hain.
no: Right middle cerebral artery || Right middle cerebral artery || MCA weakens the face and arm more than the leg, and the language or attention deficits dominate. || MCA chehra aur bazoo ko taang se zyada kamzor karta hai aur zubaan ya attention ke nuqs numaya hotay hain.
no: Left posterior cerebral artery || Left posterior cerebral artery || PCA mainly gives visual field loss and thalamic sensory signs, with strength usually preserved. || PCA aam taur par nazar ke field ki kami aur thalamic sensory alamat deta hai, taqat aksar bachi rehti hai.
hint: Think legs first: which territory sits on the inner (medial) surface? || Pehle taang sochein: kaunsa territory andar wali (medial) surface par hai?
say: **Which hemisphere?** In most people the **left hemisphere is dominant for language**. A left MCA stroke therefore tends to give aphasia (trouble speaking or understanding) and apraxia, on top of the right-sided weakness. The **right hemisphere** looks after spatial attention and awareness of the body. A right MCA stroke tends to give **neglect** (the person ignores the left side of space and body), poor insight into the weakness (anosognosia) and spatial errors, so these patients often do not know they are ill. || **Kaunsa hemisphere?** Zyada tar logon mein **left hemisphere zubaan ke liye dominant** hota hai. Is liye left MCA stroke right side ki kamzori ke ilawa aksar aphasia (bolne ya samajhne mein mushkil) aur apraxia deta hai. **Right hemisphere** spatial attention aur jism ke ehsaas ko sambhalta hai. Right MCA stroke aksar **neglect** (mareez space ki aur jism ki left side ko nazar-andaz karta hai), kamzori ka ehsaas na hona (anosognosia) aur spatial ghaltiyan deta hai, is liye in mareezon ko aksar pata hi nahi hota ke woh bimar hain.
check: Mrs K, 68, has a stroke. She eats only the food on the right half of her plate, never looks to the left, and says "my left arm is fine" while it hangs limp. Which side is the damaged hemisphere? || Mrs K, 68, ko stroke hota hai. Woh sirf plate ke right hisse ka khana khati hai, kabhi left nahi dekhti aur kehti hai "mera left bazoo theek hai" jabke woh dhila latka hai. Kaunsa hemisphere mutasir hai?
ok: Right hemisphere (right MCA): neglect and anosognosia of the left side || Right hemisphere (right MCA): left side ka neglect aur anosognosia || Yes — the right hemisphere builds our awareness of space and body, so damage produces neglect and lack of insight on the opposite (left) side. || Haan — right hemisphere space aur jism ka ehsaas banata hai, is liye nuqsan ulti (left) side ka neglect aur insight ki kami paida karta hai.
no: Left hemisphere (left MCA): aphasia || Left hemisphere (left MCA): aphasia || A left hemisphere stroke would give right-sided weakness and aphasia; she has left-sided signs and neglect. || Left hemisphere stroke right-sided kamzori aur aphasia deta; is mein left-sided alamat aur neglect hai.
no: Brainstem: lateral medullary syndrome || Brainstem: lateral medullary syndrome || A medullary stroke gives vertigo, swallowing trouble and crossed sensory loss, not neglect. || Medullary stroke chakkar, nigalne ki mushkil aur crossed sensory loss deta hai, neglect nahi.
memory: **"MCA is Mouth and hAnd; ACA is Ankle and Apathy; PCA is Peepers."** MCA: face and arm worse than leg, plus language (left) or neglect (right). ACA: leg worse than arm, plus apathy and bladder. PCA: eyes (visual field) and thalamic sensation. || **"MCA Munh aur haath; ACA Ankle aur Apathy; PCA Peepers (aankhein)."** MCA: chehra aur bazoo taang se zyada, saath zubaan (left) ya neglect (right). ACA: taang bazoo se zyada, saath bedili aur bladder. PCA: aankhein (visual field) aur thalamic sensation.
compare: Cortical strokes at a glance || Cortical strokes ek nazar mein
head: Artery || Artery ;; Typical findings (opposite body) || Aam findings (ulti side ka jism) ;; Physiotherapy twist || Physiotherapy ka mod
row: MCA (lateral cortex) || MCA (lateral cortex) ;; Face and arm weaker than leg; sensory loss; hemianopia; left side: aphasia; right side: neglect || Chehra aur bazoo taang se zyada kamzor; sensory kami; hemianopia; left: aphasia; right: neglect ;; Protect the shoulder, early arm practice, scan cueing for neglect, gesture-led teaching for aphasia || Kandhe ki hifazat, bazoo ki jaldi mashq, neglect ke liye scanning cue, aphasia ke liye ishaaron wali taleem
row: ACA (medial cortex) || ACA (medial cortex) ;; Leg and foot weaker than arm; apathy, slow to start; incontinence; grasp reflex || Taang aur paaon bazoo se zyada kamzor; bedili, shuru karne mein susti; incontinence; grasp reflex ;; Gait and stance first; external cues and rhythm to start movement; report bladder issues || Pehle chaal aur stance; harkat shuru karne ke liye bahari cues aur rhythm; bladder ke masle batayein
row: PCA (occipital and thalamus) || PCA (occipital aur thalamus) ;; Homonymous hemianopia; thalamic sensory loss or burning pain; strength usually normal || Homonymous hemianopia; thalamic sensory kami ya jalan wala dard; taqat aksar normal ;; Visual scanning, clear the blind side, sensory re-education, explain central pain || Visual scanning, andhi side saaf rakhein, sensory re-education, central pain samjhayein
check: A patient has sudden vertigo and vomiting, a hoarse voice and difficulty swallowing, loses pain and temperature on the RIGHT side of the face and the LEFT side of the body, and has a small right pupil. Where is the lesion? || Mareez ko achanak chakkar aur ulti, bhari awaaz, nigalne mein mushkil, chehre ki RIGHT side aur jism ki LEFT side par dard aur temperature ghayab, aur right pupil chhoti hai. Lesion kahan hai?
ok: Right lateral medulla (Wallenberg: PICA or vertebral artery) || Right lateral medulla (Wallenberg: PICA ya vertebral artery) || Yes — face on the lesion side and body on the opposite side is the crossed pattern unique to the lateral medulla. The small pupil is Horner's syndrome on the same side. || Haan — chehra lesion ki side aur jism doosri side crossed pattern hai jo sirf lateral medulla ka khaas hai. Chhoti pupil usi side ka Horner's syndrome hai.
no: Left MCA || Left MCA || MCA gives weakness and language problems with the face and body on the same (opposite) side, no crossing. || MCA kamzori aur zubaan ke masail deta hai, chehra aur jism ek hi (ulti) side par, crossing nahi.
no: Left ACA || Left ACA || ACA gives leg weakness and apathy, not vertigo and crossed sensory loss. || ACA taang ki kamzori aur bedili deta hai, chakkar aur crossed sensory loss nahi.
mistake: **Treating dizziness as "just vertigo".** A posterior-circulation stroke (the brainstem or cerebellum) can look like a harmless inner-ear problem: vertigo, nausea, a wobbly gait and little else. Strength may be normal and the scan can even be normal early. Any sudden vertigo with a new headache, double vision, slurred speech, facial numbness, trouble swallowing or an inability to walk unaided is a stroke until proven otherwise. The second trap is to focus only on strength: stroke also takes vision, sensation, attention, language and swallowing. || **Chakkar ko "sirf vertigo" samajhna.** Posterior-circulation stroke (brainstem ya cerebellum) bezarar andaruni kaan ke masle jaisa lag sakta hai: chakkar, matli, larkhadati chaal aur bas. Taqat normal ho sakti hai aur shuru mein scan bhi normal aa sakta hai. Achanak chakkar ke saath naya sar dard, double vision, lukhnat, chehre ka sunn hona, nigalne mein mushkil ya baghair sahare chal na paana, jab tak ghalat sabit na ho, stroke hai. Doosra jaal: sirf taqat par tawajjo dena: stroke nazar, sensation, attention, zubaan aur nigalna bhi cheen leta hai.
steps: Suspected stroke in the clinic: act in this order || Clinic mein stroke ka shak: is tarteeb se amal karein
step: Spot it with BE-FAST :: Sudden loss of Balance, Eyes (vision loss or double vision), Face droop, Arm weakness, Speech trouble, then note the Time it started. || BE-FAST se pehchanein :: Achanak Balance ki kami, Eyes (nazar jana ya double vision), Face latakna, Arm ki kamzori, Speech ka masla, phir shuru hone ka Waqt likhein.
step: Call for emergency help at once :: Do not wait to see if it settles. Clot-busting drugs and clot retrieval only work in a narrow time window. || Foran emergency madad bulayein :: Intezaar na karein ke theek ho jaye. Clot todne wali dawaiyan aur clot nikalne ka tareeqa sirf tang waqt ke andar kaam karte hain.
step: Note the exact time last seen well :: The medical team needs it to decide on treatment. || Aakhri baar theek dekhne ka sahi waqt likhein :: Medical team ko ilaaj tay karne ke liye yeh chahiye.
step: Keep them safe and still :: Lie them down or sit them supported, nothing to eat or drink (swallowing may be impaired), do not give aspirin unless a doctor says so. || Mehfooz aur sakit rakhein :: Litayein ya sahare se baithayein, khana peena kuch nahi (nigalna mutasir ho sakta hai), doctor ke kehne ke baghair aspirin na dein.
step: Stay with them and watch :: Note changes in speech, strength and alertness until help arrives. || Un ke saath rahein aur nazar rakhein :: Madad aane tak bolne, taqat aur hoshyari ki tabdeeli note karein.
sort: Cortical stroke or deep (lacunar) stroke? Sort the clue. || Cortical stroke ya deep (lacunar) stroke? Ishara sort karein.
cats: Cortical (MCA, ACA, PCA) || Cortical (MCA, ACA, PCA) ;; Deep small vessel (lacunar) || Gehri chhoti nali (lacunar)
item: Aphasia || Aphasia || 0 || Language is a cortical job, so aphasia means the cortex is involved. || Zubaan cortex ka kaam hai, is liye aphasia ka matlab cortex mutasir hai.
item: Neglect of one side of space || Space ki ek side ka neglect || 0 || Spatial attention is built by the cortex, mainly the right hemisphere. || Spatial attention cortex banata hai, khaas kar right hemisphere.
item: Visual field loss || Visual field ki kami || 0 || The visual pathway ends in the occipital cortex, so field loss points to a PCA (or MCA) cortical lesion. || Nazar ka raasta occipital cortex par khatam hota hai, is liye field ki kami PCA (ya MCA) cortical lesion ki taraf ishara hai.
item: Face, arm and leg equally weak, with a clear mind and no field loss || Chehra, bazoo aur taang barabar kamzor, zehn saaf aur field ki kami nahi || 1 || Equal weakness with no cortical signs means the fibres are squeezed together in a small deep area such as the internal capsule. || Barabar kamzori aur cortical alamaat nahi: fibres kisi chhoti gehri jagah jaise internal capsule mein tang hain.
item: Pure sensory loss on one side of the body || Jism ki ek side par sirf sensory kami || 1 || A tiny thalamic lacune gives a pure sensory stroke. || Chhota thalamic lacune pure sensory stroke deta hai.
clinic: **Treat the pattern, not the label.** For the MCA stroke with neglect: place the call bell, the TV and visitors on the neglected side, start the scan from the affected side with a coloured anchor, and measure progress with a line-bisection or star-cancellation task. For aphasia: short sentences, one idea at a time, demonstrate rather than explain, and test comprehension separately from speech: many aphasic patients understand far more than they can say. Protect the hemiplegic shoulder in every transfer: never pull on the arm. || **Label nahi, pattern ka ilaaj karein.** Neglect wale MCA stroke mein: call bell, TV aur mulaqati neglected side par rakhein, scan ko rang ke anchor ke saath mutasir side se shuru karwayein, aur line-bisection ya star-cancellation task se progress naapein. Aphasia mein: chhote jumlay, ek waqt mein ek khayal, samjhane ki bajaye dikhayein, aur samajh ko bolne se alag test karein: kai aphasic mareez bolne se kahin zyada samajhte hain. Har transfer mein hemiplegic kandhe ki hifazat karein: bazoo ko kabhi na kheenchein.
evidence: The Oxford Community Stroke Project (OCSP) classification sorts strokes by their bedside pattern: **total anterior (TACS)**, **partial anterior (PACS)**, **lacunar (LACS)** and **posterior circulation (POCS)** syndromes, and it predicts outcome and recurrence reasonably well. On timing: the **AVERT** trial found that starting very high-dose mobilisation within 24 hours after stroke did NOT improve outcome at 3 months and made a good outcome less likely than usual care, so more and earlier is not always better; follow the medical team's pace and focus on frequent, short, supervised sessions out of bed. || Oxford Community Stroke Project (OCSP) classification strokes ko bistar ke pattern se sort karti hai: **total anterior (TACS)**, **partial anterior (PACS)**, **lacunar (LACS)** aur **posterior circulation (POCS)**, aur yeh outcome aur dobara hone ka theek andaza deti hai. Waqt ke bare mein: **AVERT** trial mein pata chala ke stroke ke 24 ghantay ke andar bohat zyada dose wali mobilisation shuru karne se 3 mahine ka outcome behtar NAHI hua aur aam care ke muqable mein achha outcome kam mumkin hua, is liye zyada aur jaldi hamesha behtar nahi; medical team ki raftaar follow karein aur bistar se bahar, kam waqt ke magar baar baar, nigrani wale sessions par tawajjo dein.
safety: **A change after the first stroke is an emergency:** new or worsening weakness, speech change, severe headache, drowsiness or a sudden drop in consciousness during a session means stop, lie the patient safe and call for medical help. Before mobilising early after a stroke, check the blood pressure and heart rate against the team's limits, and screen swallowing before any food or drink. Hold exercise if the patient is unwell or the blood pressure is outside the limits. || **Pehle stroke ke baad koi tabdeeli emergency hai:** session ke dauran nayi ya barhti kamzori, bolne mein tabdeeli, shadeed sar dard, neend ya hoshyari mein achanak kami ka matlab hai ruk jayein, mareez ko mehfooz litayein aur medical madad bulayein. Stroke ke baad jaldi mobilise karne se pehle blood pressure aur heart rate ko team ki hadood se milayein, aur koi khana ya peena dene se pehle nigalne ki screening karein. Mareez bimar ho ya blood pressure hadood se bahar ho to exercise rok dein.
check: Why is the hemiparetic (weak-sided) shoulder vulnerable during transfers? || Transfers ke dauran hemiparetic (kamzor side ka) kandha kyun nazuk hota hai?
ok: The muscles that hold the humeral head in the socket are weak and the arm hangs, so pulling on it can subluxate or injure the joint || Humeral head ko socket mein rakhne wale muscles kamzor hain aur bazoo latka hota hai, is liye kheenchne se joint subluxate ya zakhmi ho sakta hai || Yes — the passive restraints take the load, so the arm must be supported, never pulled. || Haan — passive restraints bojh uthate hain, is liye bazoo ko sahara dein, kabhi na kheenchein.
no: Because the shoulder is always stiff after a stroke || Kyunke stroke ke baad kandha hamesha sakht hota hai || Early on, the arm is often flaccid, not stiff, which is exactly why it is vulnerable. || Shuru mein bazoo aksar dhila (flaccid) hota hai, sakht nahi, aur isi wajah se nazuk hota hai.
no: Because patients with stroke cannot feel their shoulders at all || Kyunke stroke ke mareez apne kandhon ko bilkul mehsoos nahi karte || Sensation varies; the main risk is the loss of muscle support, not total numbness. || Sensation mukhtalif hoti hai; asal khatra muscle ke sahare ki kami hai, mukammal sunn hona nahi.
reveal: Why does a PCA stroke often leave strength normal, even though it is a "big" stroke? || PCA stroke "bara" stroke hone ke baawajood taqat aksar normal kyun chhor deta hai? || The PCA feeds the **occipital lobe** (vision), the **thalamus** (sensory relay) and parts of the temporal lobe, not the motor strip. The strength pathway sits in the MCA and ACA territory. Weakness appears only if the PCA stroke reaches the midbrain (the cerebral peduncle) or the internal capsule, which is why PCA strokes are often missed or mistaken for "just confusion" or an eye problem. || PCA **occipital lobe** (nazar), **thalamus** (sensory relay) aur temporal lobe ke kuch hisson ko khoon deti hai, motor strip ko nahi. Taqat ka raasta MCA aur ACA territory mein hai. Kamzori tab hoti hai jab PCA stroke midbrain (cerebral peduncle) ya internal capsule tak pohanche, isi liye PCA strokes aksar chhoot jate hain ya "sirf confusion" ya aankh ka masla samjhay jate hain.
summary: Each artery has a fingerprint: MCA = face and arm plus language (left) or neglect (right); ACA = leg plus apathy and bladder; PCA = vision and thalamic sensation; lateral medulla = crossed face and body; lacunar = equal weakness with a clear mind. || Har artery ka fingerprint hai: MCA = chehra aur bazoo, saath zubaan (left) ya neglect (right); ACA = taang, saath bedili aur bladder; PCA = nazar aur thalamic sensation; lateral medulla = crossed chehra aur jism; lacunar = barabar kamzori, zehn saaf.
summary: Left hemisphere is usually the language side; the right looks after attention and body awareness, so right strokes often hide the illness from the patient. || Left hemisphere aam taur par zubaan ki side hai; right attention aur jism ke ehsaas ko sambhalta hai, is liye right strokes aksar bimari mareez se chhupa dete hain.
summary: Sudden dizziness plus brainstem signs is a stroke until proven otherwise: use BE-FAST, call for help, and protect the weak shoulder and the swallow. || Achanak chakkar aur brainstem ki alamat jab tak ghalat sabit na ho stroke hai: BE-FAST istemal karein, madad bulayein, aur kamzor kandhe aur nigalne ki hifazat karein.
card: What does an MCA stroke typically cause? || MCA stroke aam taur par kya karta hai? || Opposite face and arm weakness (more than the leg), sensory loss, hemianopia; aphasia if left, neglect if right. || Ulti side chehra aur bazoo ki kamzori (taang se zyada), sensory kami, hemianopia; left mein aphasia, right mein neglect.
card: What does an ACA stroke typically cause? || ACA stroke aam taur par kya karta hai? || Opposite leg weakness greater than the arm, apathy or abulia, urinary incontinence. || Ulti taang ki kamzori bazoo se zyada, bedili ya abulia, peshab ka na rukna.
card: What does a PCA stroke typically cause? || PCA stroke aam taur par kya karta hai? || Opposite homonymous hemianopia, possible thalamic sensory loss or pain; strength usually spared. || Ulti homonymous hemianopia, mumkin thalamic sensory kami ya dard; taqat aksar bachi rehti hai.
card: What is the lateral medullary (Wallenberg) pattern? || Lateral medullary (Wallenberg) pattern kya hai? || Vertigo, dysphagia, same-side Horner's and face pain/temperature loss, opposite-side body pain/temperature loss. || Chakkar, dysphagia, usi side Horner's aur chehre ke dard/temperature ki kami, ulti side jism ke dard/temperature ki kami.
card: What does BE-FAST stand for? || BE-FAST ka matlab kya hai? || Balance, Eyes, Face, Arm, Speech, Time: any sudden sign means call emergency help now. || Balance, Eyes, Face, Arm, Speech, Time: koi achanak alamat ho to foran emergency madad bulayein.
deeper: Stroke rehabilitation guide || /conditions/stroke-rehabilitation || The staged rehabilitation guide after stroke. || Stroke ke baad marhala-war rehabilitation guide.
deeper: UMN vs LMN lesson || /learn/umn-vs-lmn || The signs that follow a cortical or cord lesion. || Cortical ya cord lesion ke baad ki alamaat.
deeper: Motor learning and neuroplasticity || /learn/motor-learning-neuroplasticity || How repeated, task-specific practice rewires the brain after a stroke. || Baar baar task-specific mashq stroke ke baad dimagh ko kaise dobara tarteeb deti hai.
source: Bamford J, Sandercock P, Dennis M, Burn J, Warlow C. Classification and natural history of clinically identifiable subtypes of cerebral infarction. Lancet. 1991;337:1521–1526. || classification natural history clinically identifiable subtypes cerebral infarction
source: AVERT Trial Collaboration Group. Efficacy and safety of very early mobilisation within 24 h of stroke onset (AVERT): a randomised controlled trial. Lancet. 2015;386:46–55. || AVERT very early mobilisation within 24 h of stroke onset randomised
